A rectangle with length $(x+a)$ and width $(x+b)$ has area $(x+a)(x+b)$ — a binomial product.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[thick, blue!70!black] (0,0) rectangle (7,3.2);
\node[above] at (3.5,3.2) {$x+a$};
\node[left] at (0,1.6) {$x+b$};
\node at (3.5,1.6) {Area $=(x+a)(x+b)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

When a border of width $x$ runs all the way around a rectangle, each dimension changes by $2x$, not by $x$. Here $p$ and $q$ are the inner rectangle's length and width.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[thick, blue!70!black] (0,0) rectangle (7,4.4);
\filldraw[thick, blue!70!black, fill=blue!15] (1.1,1.1) rectangle (5.9,3.3);
\node at (3.5,2.85) {$p$};
\node at (1.65,2.2) {$q$};
\draw[<->, thick] (0,2.2) -- (1.1,2.2);
\node[above] at (0.55,2.2) {$x$};
\draw[<->, thick] (5.9,2.2) -- (7,2.2);
\node[above] at (6.45,2.2) {$x$};
\draw[<->, thick] (3.5,3.3) -- (3.5,4.4);
\node[right] at (3.5,3.85) {$x$};
\draw[<->, thick] (3.5,0) -- (3.5,1.1);
\node[right] at (3.5,0.55) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
The outside edge of a path around a rectangular pool measures $20$ m by $12$ m. The path is $x$ m wide all the way around. Write an expanded expression for the pool area.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black,thick] (0,0) rectangle (6,3.6);
\draw[black,thick] (0.8,0.8) rectangle (5.2,2.8);
\path (3,3.6) node[above] {$20\text{ m}$};
\path (6,1.8) node[right] {$12\text{ m}$};
\path (3,1.8) node {Pool};
\draw[black,<->] (0,1.8)--(0.8,1.8);
\path (0.4,1.8) node[above] {$x$};
\draw[black,<->] (3,2.8)--(3,3.6);
\path (3,3.2) node[right] {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
